1.1 Analytics architecture principles
Moment-first and user-aware: every important behavior should be analyzable from both the user and Moment perspective.
Meaningful actions are more important than clicks. Screen views diagnose UX; they do not prove product value.
Backend owns persisted business truth; frontend owns views, attempts and navigation; system/state engine owns lifecycle transitions.
Analytics is non-blocking. A telemetry failure must never cause Moment creation, joining, contribution or completion to fail.
Raw events are append-oriented behavioral history. KPIs are derived centrally and versioned.
Personal, Group and Business remain dimensions of the same analytics model, not separate event universes.
No raw PII or user free text is written to standard analytics payloads.
Every rate stores numerator and denominator so sample size is always visible.
1.2 End-to-end analytical story
Acquisition / Invite        ↓user_registered        ↓create OR join Moment        ↓qualifying meaningful activity        ↓User Activated        ↓Moment Activated / WAM        ↓Moment Completed        ↓Second Moment        ↓Participant becomes Creator        ↓New Moment + New Participants

