7. Migration SQL V059–V068
The SQL below is an implementation baseline. It should be applied through the same migration mechanism used for Momentra V001–V058. Pack script names map to repository files V059–V068 (V031–V040 version numbers are already used by unrelated product migrations). Database role creation may require elevated privileges; where Supabase/hosting policy manages roles externally, keep schema grants but provision roles through the environment instead.
V059__lean_analytics_schemas_and_roles.sql
BEGIN;CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS analytics_raw;CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS analytics_core;CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS analytics_mart;-- Roles are optional when deployment IAM/role management is external.DO $$ BEGIN  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='analytics_ingest') THEN CREATE ROLE analytics_ingest NOLOGIN; END IF;  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='analytics_transform') THEN CREATE ROLE analytics_transform NOLOGIN; END IF;  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='analytics_read') THEN CREATE ROLE analytics_read NOLOGIN; END IF;EXCEPTION WHEN insufficient_privilege THEN  RAISE NOTICE 'Role creation skipped: insufficient privilege';END $$;REVOKE ALL ON SCHEMA analytics_raw, analytics_core, analytics_mart FROM PUBLIC;GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA analytics_raw TO analytics_ingest, analytics_transform;GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA analytics_core, analytics_mart TO analytics_transform, analytics_read;COMMIT;

