9.3 Transformation pattern — user_daily
INSERT INTO analytics_core.user_daily (  activity_date,user_id,session_count,screen_view_count,moments_created,moments_joined,moments_viewed,  meaningful_action_count,expenses_added,contributions_recorded,invites_sent,moments_completed,active_flag,meaningfully_active_flag)SELECT  (e.occurred_at AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Kolkata')::date AS activity_date,  e.user_id,  COUNT(DISTINCT e.session_id) FILTER (WHERE e.session_id IS NOT NULL),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='screen_viewed'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='moment_created'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='participant_joined'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='moment_viewed'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name IN ('moment_created','participant_invited','participant_joined','expense_added','contribution_recorded','split_created','memory_created','moment_completed') OR (e.event_name='moment_activity_completed' AND a.activity_type IS NOT NULL)),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='expense_added'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='contribution_recorded'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='participant_invited'),  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE e.event_name='moment_completed'),  TRUE,  BOOL_OR(e.event_name IN ('moment_created','participant_invited','participant_joined','expense_added','contribution_recorded','split_created','memory_created','moment_completed') OR (e.event_name='moment_activity_completed' AND a.activity_type IS NOT NULL))FROM analytics_raw.events eLEFT JOIN analytics_core.activity_type_registry a  ON a.activity_type = e.properties->>'activity_type' AND a.is_meaningful AND a.active_from <= e.occurred_at AND (a.active_to IS NULL OR a.active_to > e.occurred_at)WHERE e.is_valid AND e.user_id IS NOT NULL  AND e.occurred_at >= :from_ts AND e.occurred_at < :to_tsGROUP BY 1,2ON CONFLICT (activity_date,user_id) DO UPDATE SET  session_count=EXCLUDED.session_count, screen_view_count=EXCLUDED.screen_view_count,  moments_created=EXCLUDED.moments_created, moments_joined=EXCLUDED.moments_joined,  moments_viewed=EXCLUDED.moments_viewed, meaningful_action_count=EXCLUDED.meaningful_action_count,  expenses_added=EXCLUDED.expenses_added, contributions_recorded=EXCLUDED.contributions_recorded,  invites_sent=EXCLUDED.invites_sent, moments_completed=EXCLUDED.moments_completed,  active_flag=EXCLUDED.active_flag, meaningfully_active_flag=EXCLUDED.meaningfully_active_flag, updated_at=now();

10. KPI SQL Reference — 42 KPIs
These are calculation templates. Production jobs should parameterize period boundaries and write finalized outputs to analytics_mart.kpi_period. Queries use Asia/Kolkata business-day boundaries where relevant; raw storage remains UTC.
1. New Registered Users
Definition: Count of distinct users successfully registered in the reporting period.
Formula: Count(distinct user_id with registered_at in period)
Reference SQL — KPI_001_NEW_REGISTERED_USERS
SELECT COUNT(*) AS value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at >= :start_ts AND registered_at < :end_ts;

2. User Growth Rate
Definition: Growth in new registrations versus the previous comparable period.
Formula: (Current new users - Previous new users) / Previous new users
Reference SQL — KPI_002_USER_GROWTH_RATE
WITH c AS (SELECT COUNT(*)::numeric n FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:start_ts AND registered_at<:end_ts), p AS (SELECT COUNT(*)::numeric n FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:prev_start_ts AND registered_at<:prev_end_ts) SELECT (c.n-p.n)*100.0/NULLIF(p.n,0) AS value FROM c,p;

3. Acquisition Source Mix
Definition: Distribution of new registered users by acquisition source.
Formula: New users by source / all new users
Reference SQL — KPI_003_ACQUISITION_SOURCE_MIX
SELECT COALESCE(acquisition_source,'unknown') source, COUNT(*) users, 100.0*COUNT(*)/SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER() pct FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:start_ts AND registered_at<:end_ts GROUP BY 1;

4. Invite-Sourced Users
Definition: New registered users attributable to Moment invitations.
Formula: Count(users with invite_sourced_flag=true)
Reference SQL — KPI_004_INVITE_SOURCED_USERS
SELECT COUNT(*) AS value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:start_ts AND registered_at<:end_ts AND invite_sourced_flag;

5. Activated Acquisition Rate
Definition: Share of eligible new users who activate within 14 days.
Formula: Activated eligible new users / eligible new registered users
Reference SQL — KPI_005_ACTIVATED_ACQUISITION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE activated_at IS NOT NULL AND activated_at<=registered_at+INTERVAL '14 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:cohort_start AND registered_at<:cohort_end AND registered_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '14 days';

6. User Activation Rate
Definition: User creates or joins a Moment and performs a subsequent qualifying Moment activity within 14 days of registration.
Formula: Activated users / eligible registered users
Reference SQL — KPI_006_USER_ACTIVATION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE activated_at IS NOT NULL AND activated_at<=registered_at+INTERVAL '14 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE registered_at>=:cohort_start AND registered_at<:cohort_end AND registered_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '14 days';

7. Median Time to First Moment
Definition: Median elapsed time from registration to first Moment created.
Formula: median(first_moment_created_at - registered_at)
Reference SQL — KPI_007_MEDIAN_TIME_TO_FIRST_MOMENT
SELECT percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (first_moment_created_at-registered_at))) value_seconds FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE first_moment_created_at IS NOT NULL;

8. Median Time to First Meaningful Action
Definition: Median elapsed time from registration to first qualifying meaningful activity.
Formula: median(first_meaningful_action_at - registered_at)
Reference SQL — KPI_008_MEDIAN_TIME_TO_FIRST_MEANINGFUL_ACTION
SELECT percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (first_meaningful_action_at-registered_at))) value_seconds FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE first_meaningful_action_at IS NOT NULL;

9. Moment Creation Completion Rate
Definition: Share of creation-flow instances that successfully persist a Moment.
Formula: created creation_flow_id / started creation_flow_id
Reference SQL — KPI_009_MOMENT_CREATION_COMPLETION_RATE
WITH s AS (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT properties->>'creation_flow_id') n FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='moment_creation_started' AND occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts), c AS (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT properties->>'creation_flow_id') n FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='moment_created' AND occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts) SELECT c.n*100.0/NULLIF(s.n,0) value FROM s,c;

10. Moment Creation Drop-Off
Definition: Loss between consecutive creation steps.
Formula: 1 - step_n_flows / step_n_minus_1_flows
Reference SQL — KPI_010_MOMENT_CREATION_DROP_OFF
SELECT properties->>'step_name' step_name, COUNT(DISTINCT properties->>'creation_flow_id') flows FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='moment_creation_step_completed' AND occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN((properties->>'step_number')::int);

11. Join Activation Rate
Definition: Joined invited users who perform a qualifying Moment activity within 7 days.
Formula: activated joined invitees / eligible joined invitees
Reference SQL — KPI_011_JOIN_ACTIVATION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE participant_activated_at IS NOT NULL AND participant_activated_at<=joined_at+INTERVAL '7 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.participant_fact WHERE joined_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '7 days';

12. Moments Created
Definition: Distinct Moments successfully persisted in period.
Formula: count(distinct moment_id created)
Reference SQL — KPI_012_MOMENTS_CREATED
SELECT COUNT(*) value FROM analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact WHERE created_at>=:start_ts AND created_at<:end_ts;

13. Weekly Active Moments (WAM)
Definition: Distinct Moments with at least one post-creation qualifying activity in the week. Creation/view alone does not qualify.
Formula: count(distinct meaningfully active moment_id)
Reference SQL — KPI_013_WEEKLY_ACTIVE_MOMENTS_WAM
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT moment_id) value FROM analytics_core.moment_daily WHERE activity_date>=:week_start AND activity_date<:week_start+7 AND meaningfully_active_flag;

14. Monthly Active Moments (MAM)
Definition: Distinct Moments with at least one qualifying activity in the calendar month.
Formula: count(distinct meaningfully active moment_id)
Reference SQL — KPI_014_MONTHLY_ACTIVE_MOMENTS_MAM
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT moment_id) value FROM analytics_core.moment_daily WHERE activity_date>=:month_start AND activity_date<:month_end AND meaningfully_active_flag;

15. Moments per Active User
Definition: Average distinct meaningfully active Moment-user relationships per meaningfully active user.
Formula: active moment-user relationships / meaningfully active users
Reference SQL — KPI_015_MOMENTS_PER_ACTIVE_USER
WITH active_users AS (SELECT DISTINCT user_id FROM analytics_core.user_daily WHERE activity_date>=:start_date AND activity_date<:end_date AND meaningfully_active_flag), pairs AS (SELECT DISTINCT e.moment_id, e.user_id FROM analytics_raw.events e LEFT JOIN analytics_core.activity_type_registry a ON a.activity_type = e.properties->>'activity_type' AND a.is_meaningful AND (a.active_to IS NULL OR a.active_to > e.occurred_at) AND a.active_from <= e.occurred_at WHERE e.is_valid AND e.user_id IS NOT NULL AND e.moment_id IS NOT NULL AND e.occurred_at>=:start_ts AND e.occurred_at<:end_ts AND (e.event_name IN ('moment_created','participant_invited','participant_joined','expense_added','contribution_recorded','split_created','memory_created','moment_completed') OR (e.event_name='moment_activity_completed' AND a.activity_type IS NOT NULL))) SELECT COUNT(*)::numeric/NULLIF((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM active_users),0) value FROM pairs;

16. Moment Activation Rate
Definition: Created Moments reaching the backend-defined activation state within the V1 7-day maturity window.
Formula: activated eligible Moments / eligible created Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_016_MOMENT_ACTIVATION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE activated_at IS NOT NULL AND activated_at<=created_at+INTERVAL '7 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact WHERE created_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '7 days' AND NOT is_cancelled;

17. Moment Completion Rate
Definition: Mature activated Moments reaching valid completion; V1 maturity window 30 days.
Formula: completed mature activated / mature activated
Reference SQL — KPI_017_MOMENT_COMPLETION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE completed_at IS NOT NULL)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact WHERE activated_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '30 days' AND NOT is_cancelled;

18. Meaningful Actions per Active Moment
Definition: Depth of orchestration inside active Moments.
Formula: qualifying activity events / active Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_018_MEANINGFUL_ACTIONS_PER_ACTIVE_MOMENT
SELECT SUM(meaningful_action_count)::numeric/NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT moment_id),0) value FROM analytics_core.moment_daily WHERE activity_date>=:start_date AND activity_date<:end_date AND meaningfully_active_flag;

19. Meaningful Actions per Active User
Definition: Average qualifying actions performed by meaningfully active users.
Formula: qualifying actions / meaningfully active users
Reference SQL — KPI_019_MEANINGFUL_ACTIONS_PER_ACTIVE_USER
SELECT SUM(meaningful_action_count)::numeric/NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) FILTER(WHERE meaningfully_active_flag),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_daily WHERE activity_date>=:start_date AND activity_date<:end_date;

20. Average Participants per Group Moment
Definition: Average active participant relationships per eligible Group Moment.
Formula: active participants / Group Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_020_AVERAGE_PARTICIPANTS_PER_GROUP_MOMENT
SELECT AVG(cnt)::numeric value FROM (SELECT moment_id,COUNT(*) cnt FROM analytics_core.participant_fact pf JOIN analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact mf USING(moment_id) WHERE mf.moment_domain='group' AND pf.is_active_participant GROUP BY moment_id) x;

21. Moment Revisit Rate
Definition: Eligible Moments viewed in a later session after first qualifying view.
Formula: revisited Moments / eligible viewed Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_021_MOMENT_REVISIT_RATE
WITH v AS (SELECT moment_id,COUNT(DISTINCT session_id) sessions FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='moment_viewed' AND is_valid GROUP BY moment_id) SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE sessions>=2)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM v;

22. Moment Type / Category Mix
Definition: Distribution of created Moments by domain/category/type.
Formula: created Moments of segment / all created Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_022_MOMENT_TYPE__CATEGORY_MIX
SELECT moment_domain,moment_category,moment_type,COUNT(*) moments,100.0*COUNT(*)/SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER() pct FROM analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact WHERE created_at>=:start_ts AND created_at<:end_ts GROUP BY 1,2,3;

23. D7 Meaningful Retention
Definition: Activated cohort users with meaningful activity during D7–D9.
Formula: D7-D9 retained / eligible activated cohort
Reference SQL — KPI_023_D7_MEANINGFUL_RETENTION
SELECT d7_rate value FROM analytics_mart.user_retention_cohort WHERE cohort_type='activation' AND cohort_date=:cohort_date AND formula_version=1;

24. D30 Meaningful Retention
Definition: Activated cohort users with meaningful activity during D30–D36.
Formula: D30-D36 retained / eligible activated cohort
Reference SQL — KPI_024_D30_MEANINGFUL_RETENTION
SELECT d30_rate value FROM analytics_mart.user_retention_cohort WHERE cohort_type='activation' AND cohort_date=:cohort_date AND formula_version=1;

25. Second Moment Rate
Definition: First-time creators who create a second Moment within 60 days.
Formula: 2nd Moment creators / mature first-time creator cohort
Reference SQL — KPI_025_SECOND_MOMENT_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE second_moment_created_at IS NOT NULL AND second_moment_created_at<=first_moment_created_at+INTERVAL '60 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE first_moment_created_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '60 days';

26. Repeat Moment Creator Rate
Definition: Current eligible creator population with at least two created Moments.
Formula: creators with >=2 Moments / eligible creators
Reference SQL — KPI_026_REPEAT_MOMENT_CREATOR_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE total_moments_created>=2)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE total_moments_created>=1),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact;

27. Third+ Moment Creator Rate
Definition: First-time creators reaching at least three Moments within 90 days.
Formula: 3+ creators / mature first-time creator cohort
Reference SQL — KPI_027_THIRD_MOMENT_CREATOR_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE third_moment_created_at IS NOT NULL AND third_moment_created_at<=first_moment_created_at+INTERVAL '90 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE first_moment_created_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '90 days';

28. Cross-Category Adoption Rate
Definition: Repeat creators whose created Moments span at least two categories.
Formula: repeat creators across >=2 categories / repeat creators
Reference SQL — KPI_028_CROSS_CATEGORY_ADOPTION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE cross_category_flag)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE total_moments_created>=2),0) value FROM analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact WHERE total_moments_created>=2;

29. Moment Abandonment Rate
Definition: Mature created Moments that never activate and have no qualifying activity after 14 days; cancellation excluded.
Formula: abandoned / eligible created Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_029_MOMENT_ABANDONMENT_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE activated_at IS NULL AND first_meaningful_action_at IS NULL)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.moment_lifecycle_fact WHERE created_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '14 days' AND NOT is_cancelled;

30. Invitations per Group Moment
Definition: Valid invitations issued per eligible Group Moment.
Formula: distinct invite_id / eligible Group Moments
Reference SQL — KPI_030_INVITATIONS_PER_GROUP_MOMENT
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT (properties->>'invite_id'))::numeric/NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT moment_id),0) value FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='participant_invited' AND moment_domain='group' AND occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts;

31. Invite Open Rate
Definition: Unique issued invitations that are opened.
Formula: unique invite opens / valid invites issued
Reference SQL — KPI_031_INVITE_OPEN_RATE
WITH i AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'invite_id' id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='participant_invited'), o AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'invite_id' id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='invite_opened') SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM o)*100.0/NULLIF((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM i),0) value;

32. Invite → Join Conversion
Definition: Valid invitations resulting in successful participant joins within 14 days.
Formula: joined invite IDs / valid invites issued
Reference SQL — KPI_032_INVITE__JOIN_CONVERSION
WITH i AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'invite_id' id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='participant_invited' AND occurred_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '14 days'), j AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'invite_id' id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='participant_joined') SELECT COUNT(j.id)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(i.id),0) value FROM i LEFT JOIN j USING(id);

33. Invited User Activation Rate
Definition: Joined invitees who perform qualifying activity within 7 days.
Formula: activated invited users / eligible joined invited users
Reference SQL — KPI_033_INVITED_USER_ACTIVATION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE participant_activated_at IS NOT NULL AND participant_activated_at<=joined_at+INTERVAL '7 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.participant_fact WHERE joined_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '7 days';

34. Participant → Creator Conversion
Definition: Previously non-creator participants who create their first Moment within 60 days after participation.
Formula: converted participants / mature eligible participants
Reference SQL — KPI_034_PARTICIPANT__CREATOR_CONVERSION
WITH first_participation AS (SELECT user_id,MIN(joined_at) joined_at FROM analytics_core.participant_fact WHERE joined_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY user_id), eligible AS (SELECT fp.user_id,fp.joined_at,u.first_moment_created_at FROM first_participation fp JOIN analytics_core.user_lifecycle_fact u USING(user_id) WHERE fp.joined_at<=:as_of-INTERVAL '60 days' AND (u.first_moment_created_at IS NULL OR u.first_moment_created_at>fp.joined_at)) SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE first_moment_created_at<=joined_at+INTERVAL '60 days')*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM eligible;

35. Viral Coefficient
Definition: Approximate new creators generated through participation per existing creator.
Formula: invitees per creator × join rate × participant→creator rate
Reference SQL — KPI_035_VIRAL_COEFFICIENT
SELECT :invitees_per_creator * :join_rate * :participant_creator_rate AS value;

36. Quick Add Completion Rate
Definition: Quick Add flow instances reaching a successful business outcome.
Formula: completed quick-add flows / started quick-add flows
Reference SQL — KPI_036_QUICK_ADD_COMPLETION_RATE
WITH s AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'quick_add_flow_id' AS flow_id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='quick_add_started' AND is_valid AND properties->>'quick_add_flow_id' IS NOT NULL AND occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts), c AS (SELECT DISTINCT properties->>'quick_add_flow_id' AS flow_id FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE is_valid AND properties->>'quick_add_flow_id' IS NOT NULL AND event_name IN ('expense_added','contribution_recorded','moment_activity_completed')) SELECT COUNT(c.flow_id)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(s.flow_id),0) value FROM s LEFT JOIN c USING (flow_id);

37. Feature Adoption Rate
Definition: Eligible active users using a specified feature at least once.
Formula: feature users / eligible active users
Reference SQL — KPI_037_FEATURE_ADOPTION_RATE
SELECT :feature_name feature_name, COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) FILTER(WHERE event_name=:feature_event)*100.0/NULLIF(:eligible_active_users,0) value FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts;

38. Critical Flow Abandonment Rate
Definition: Critical flow instances started but not successfully completed.
Formula: abandoned flows / started flows
Reference SQL — KPI_038_CRITICAL_FLOW_ABANDONMENT_RATE
WITH s AS (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT properties->>'flow_instance_id') n FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='critical_flow_started' AND properties->>'flow_name'=:flow_name), c AS (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT properties->>'flow_instance_id') n FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE event_name='critical_flow_completed' AND properties->>'flow_name'=:flow_name) SELECT (s.n-c.n)*100.0/NULLIF(s.n,0) value FROM s,c;

39. Median Session Duration
Definition: Median elapsed time from session start to last qualifying session event.
Formula: median(last_activity - session_start)
Reference SQL — KPI_039_MEDIAN_SESSION_DURATION
SELECT percentile_cont(0.5) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY session_duration_seconds) value_seconds FROM analytics_core.session_fact WHERE session_started_at>=:start_ts AND session_started_at<:end_ts;

40. Sessions per Active User
Definition: Average distinct sessions per active user in period.
Formula: sessions / active users
Reference SQL — KPI_040_SESSIONS_PER_ACTIVE_USER
SELECT COUNT(*)::numeric/NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT user_id),0) value FROM analytics_core.session_fact WHERE session_started_at>=:start_ts AND session_started_at<:end_ts AND user_id IS NOT NULL;

41. Critical Operation Failure Rate
Definition: Failed critical operations divided by total attempts/successes+failures for that operation.
Formula: failures / operation attempts
Reference SQL — KPI_041_CRITICAL_OPERATION_FAILURE_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE event_name='critical_operation_failed' AND properties->>'operation_name'=:operation_name)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE (event_name='critical_operation_failed' AND properties->>'operation_name'=:operation_name) OR event_name=:success_event),0) value FROM analytics_raw.events WHERE occurred_at>=:start_ts AND occurred_at<:end_ts;

42. Crash-Free Session Rate
Definition: Sessions without an application crash.
Formula: non-crash sessions / total sessions
Reference SQL — KPI_042_CRASH_FREE_SESSION_RATE
SELECT COUNT(*) FILTER(WHERE NOT had_crash)*100.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) value FROM analytics_core.session_fact WHERE session_started_at>=:start_ts AND session_started_at<:end_ts;

